## UI/UX Rules
- UI must be simple and minimalist
- UX must be very intuitive and easy to use
- Design should feel "soft" — rounded corners (14-16px), subtle shadows, pastel accents
- Colors defined in AppColors (lib/core/constants/app_colors.dart)
- Theme defined in AppTheme (lib/core/constants/app_theme.dart)
- All user-facing strings in AppStrings (lib/core/constants/app_strings.dart)
- Font: Poppins via Google Fonts
- Minimum tap target: 44x44

## Coding Rules
- Do NOT change the package name (com.puzzloragames.dropzy)
- Do NOT add comments or documentation unless explicitly asked
- All new games MUST: (1) create a folder under lib/games/, (2) register in GameRegistry with builder and GameInfo, (3) use GameWrapper for lifecycle
- Use relative imports within the project (not package: imports)
- No hardcoded strings — use AppStrings
- No hardcoded colors — use AppColors
- Keep app lightweight — no heavy assets, lazy load where possible
- Portrait orientation only

## Testing
- Test files under test/screens/ (one per screen)
- Test helpers under test/helpers/
- Test all screens against 14 device sizes (7 Android + 7 iOS, from iPhone SE to iPad Pro 12.9")
- Overflow detection: tests must fail if any RenderFlex overflow occurs
- Never weaken tests to fix failures — always fix the UI code instead

## Build & Run
```bash
flutter pub get
flutter run
```

